{
  "_comment": "Copy to smoke_plan.json and adapt the names/addresses to your instance. phase: read (default) runs always; write runs only with --write and must leave the platform as found (create -> verify -> delete). Steps may capture values from JSON results and reference them as $var in later args. This example assumes devices named PE1/P1/P2/PE2 (TE router-ids 10.0.0.1/.2/.4/.3), a credential profile 'cml-xrd', an SR-PCE provider 'cml-pce' feeding CNC over gRPC with a PCC-initiated SR policy PE1<->PE2 color 100, the embedded Data Gateway and the embedded NSO provider; the write phase only touches smoke-* objects, a remove/add mapping cycle that the embedded gateway reverts by itself, NSO check-sync/sync-from/sync-to on one device, a PCE-initiated SR policy (color 200) that it creates, updates and deletes, and a no-op login-banner update, a smoke-* tag / suppression policy / device lock / location cycle, and an ack + note + un-ack on one open alarm; the cluster node id is the CNC management IP.",
